 "assumptions": [
  "Every number is from the P&ID (equipment list/connection attributes) or the operating data sheet; no project documents/datasheets exist (search_documents returned empty for three queries) and P&ID design_limits and data_quality are empty, so no site-vs-P&ID conflict arose.",
  "Unit instruction cited S315/S317/S305 as F-300 outlets, but the full P&ID and the data sheet agree S315 is F-300 broth, S305 the F-301 vent and S317 the F-300 vent; the P&ID/data sheet version was used.",
  "Exchangers H-301 and H-310 have no cited U, area or coolant rating and the data sheet gives cooling water only as 'at 28 C', so they are modelled as bare coolers to their documented outlet set points (48 C and 32 C, data sheet Design basis rows and Equipment rows) with simulator-computed duties; no area/U was invented and no U/area rating could be put in limits.",
  "Batch vessels T-310 (8x950 m3, 24 h), F-301 seed train (2x5 stages, largest 757 m3, 24 h) and F-300 (12x3600 m3, 36 h) are modelled as steady-state conversion reactors at 48 C (T-310) and 32 C (F-301/F-300) with the data sheet prescribed sugar fractions; their volumes/times are stated as mapping context, not imposed as tank limits, because the spec has no batch-reactor residence rating and hydraulics of 36/60/24 h batches cannot be checked as a continuous tank. Cooling is not a specified maximum-duty limit (no cited kW), so the simulator cooling_kW is reported, not limited.",
  "The data sheet prescribed reaction fractions are fractions of the sugar available after prior reactions; the simulator applies each conversion to the inlet of that reaction, so the entered per-reaction conversions are the sequential renormalisations (e.g. seed glucose cell mass 4% of feed = 40% of the sugar remaining after 3% lactic and 90% ethanol). Resulting total sugar consumptions match the data sheet: F-301 glucose 95.15%, xylose 90.11%; F-300 glucose 98.06%, xylose 92.92% in run area300-v4.",
  "Cellobiose is not a separate stand-in; per the data sheet reaction note 'C + 1.4696 Water -> 1.3632 G (cellulose to glucose, incl. via cellobiose)' and 'cellobiose + H2O -> 2 glucose 100% of the cellobiose', the 1.2% cellobiose route is folded into the glucose route: glucose route total 91.2% of glucan (90.0% direct + 1.2% via cellobiose), entered as 95.0% of the cellulose remaining after the 4.0% oligomer reaction.",
  "Lactic contamination (3% of glucose and xylose, data sheet) is the first reaction in both F-301 and F-300, matching 'converted to lactic acid upstream of the fermentors' in effect; Arabinose is not fermented (data sheet note) and stays in the soluble lump. The report's glycerol/succinic/xylitol reactions produce O2 as written in the data sheet stoichiometry (negative water/CO2 coefficients as given there).",
  "Pressures: feeds use data sheet pressures (S301 4.357 bar, S422 1.925, S309/S311 5.472, S310/S312 1.013, S551 4.357); T-306 is set at 1.013 bar (atmospheric beer well, assumed); T-310 and fermentor pressures follow the lowest-pressure inlet per the mixer/reactor solve. No pumps, control valves, relief valves or utility supply ratings exist on this P&ID (valves=[], control=[]), so none are modelled and no pump/valve/PSV/utility limits could be cited.",
  "check_coverage on area300-v4 flags T-310->H-310 (SACC), F-301->F-300 (S304) and F-300->T-306 (S315) as missing, but the flow demonstrably passes: SACC 443,390 kg/h enters H-310, S304 42,665 kg/h enters F-300's feed mixer, S315 424,402 kg/h enters T-306's feed mixer. A minimal diagnostic run (diag-reactor-out) proved check_coverage does not read conversion-reactor vapour/liquid ports at all, so these three flags cannot be cleared by any flowsheet change; they are a checker limitation, not missing flow."
 ],
